# TODO - Native Linux packaging

## Objective

Produce portable Linux x86-64 executables with local asset discovery.

## Acceptance

- Do not link or bundle original game executables or libraries.
- Verify startup, save paths, packaging and Linux gameplay smoke tests.
- Verify shared persistent display and input settings in native gameplay:
  resizable aspect-fit, integer scaling, fill/crop, stretch and fullscreen.
- Verify resize, high-DPI and touch-coordinate mapping across display modes.
- Verify adaptive height-fit rendering with real additional scene content,
  uniform scale and safe camera bounds. Manually adapt unsupported scenes;
  temporary aspect-fit fallback does not satisfy adaptive acceptance.
- Verify remappable per-player keyboard, mouse, controller and touch
  profiles, persistent settings and reset. Test single-player-first
  WASD/Space/left-click defaults, explicit extra-seat admission and
  one shared Escape keyboard pause control.
- Verify audible physical output and report selected audio device and
  volume controls. Dummy audio smoke does not satisfy audible acceptance.
- Verify adaptive wide scene and gameplay HUD on the owner's maximized
  desktop; keep control hints in pause/settings rather than gameplay.

- Read configured asset and executable roots from the private local .env.
- Use exactly one persistent per-title asset namespace across targets.
- Publish target-specific binaries and notices without asset copies.
- Repeat package publication must not rewrite or duplicate asset payloads.
- Migrate legacy stores only after verified consumer compatibility.

## Evidence

The selected-title release build produced an 835,768-byte dynamically
linked x86-64 ELF executable on the development host. Its direct dynamic
dependencies were SDL2, libgcc and libc; it does not use the original game
executable or library. The hidden native four-player movement smoke passed
with four verified local art bundles. This verifies local startup, not
portable distribution, independent asset discovery, saves or complete
gameplay. Those remain open.

